==Party listings==
The campaign committees for the two parties (the [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee|DCCC]] and [[National Republican Congressional Committee|NRCC]]) publish their own lists of targeted seats.

===Democratic-held seats===
The NRCC is now targeting 85 Democratic held seats.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nrcc.org/2021/11/03/nrcc-expands-offensive-map-announces-13-new-targets/|title=NRCC Expands Offensive Map, Announces 13 New Targets|date=3 November 2021}}</ref> They released their initial list February 10, 2021<ref>{{cite web|date=February 10, 2021|title=NRCC Announces 47 Offensive Pick-Up Opportunities for 2022 Cycle|url=https://www.nrcc.org/2021/02/10/nrcc-announces-47-offensive-pick-up-opportunities-for-2022-cycle/|access-date=February 22, 2021|website=NRCC}}</ref> and added 10 seats to the initial list on May 4, 2021<ref name="May4thNRCCTargets">{{cite web |title=NRCC Expands Offensive Map, Announces 10 New Targets Following Reapportionment |url=https://www.nrcc.org/2021/05/04/nrcc-expands-offensive-map-announces-10-new-targets-following-reapportionment/ |website=nrcc.org |date=4 May 2021 |publisher=NRCC |access-date=May 4, 2021}}</ref> and a further 13 seats November 3, 2021 after the favorable election night results. They added eight additional seats on March 30, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/600278-house-gop-campaign-arm-adds-new-seats-to-target-list/|title = House GOP campaign arm adds new seats to target list|date = 30 March 2022}}</ref> The first two lists were published before redistricting, but the 3rd list begins to incorporate [[2020 United States redistricting cycle|redistricting]] impacts such as Colorado's 7th congressional district. 
Seats in '''bold''' were included in the DCCC's frontline seats in March 2021 or were added in January 2022.<ref>{{cite web|date=March 1, 2021|title=Democrats to devote resources to 7 more House lawmakers facing tough re-elections|url=https://dccc.org/dccc-announces-members-of-2021-2022-frontline-program/|access-date=March 5, 2021|website=DCCC}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=January 27, 2022|title=DCCC expands list of vulnerable House Democrats|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/591613-dccc-expands-list-of-vulnerable-house-democrats|website=The Hill}}</ref>
